monk - TODO / Feature Recommendations
======================================

High priority
-------------
[ ] -e / --exit-status
      Exit non-zero when no elements are matched (like grep).
      Enables reliable use in shell scripts: if monk -f page.html "h1"; then ...

[x] -u / --url <url>
      Fetch HTML directly from a URL instead of requiring: curl <url> | monk
      Saves a very common pipe pattern.
      DONE: implemented in parse.go; Content-Type header forwarded for charset detection.

[ ] --outerhtml
      Output matched nodes as serialized HTML strings instead of the custom
      indented tree. Useful for piping output into another tool or saving
      HTML fragments.

[ ] --innerhtml
      Like --outerhtml but outputs the contents only, without the matched
      element's own opening/closing tag.

[ ] -0 / --null
      Separate output records with NUL (\0) instead of newline.
      Safe for xargs -0 piping when values may contain newlines or spaces.
      Most relevant with --attr and --text output modes.

Medium priority
---------------
[ ] ~ sibling operator
      General sibling combinator. Currently + selects the adjacent sibling;
      ~ would select all following siblings — the natural counterpart.

[ ] -q / --quiet
      Suppress all output; only set exit status (implies --exit-status).
      Pure existence check: monk -qf page.html "h1" && echo found

[ ] --pretty
      Re-serialize output as valid, indented HTML using golang.org/x/net/html
      Render. Makes output reusable as HTML, not just human-readable.

Low priority
------------
[ ] --each
      Apply a second selector to each matched node independently and flatten
      results. Different from chaining, which treats all matches as a pool.

Implementation Status
---------------------
| Feature | Implemented | Notes |
|---|---:|---|
| `-e` / `--exit-status` | No | Not currently implemented; would set exit code when no matches |
| `-u` / `--url <url>` | **Yes** | `parse.go`: HTTP GET, forwards `Content-Type` for charset detection |
| `--outerhtml` | No | Partial: `-r/--raw` exists, but not exact serialized outer HTML |
| `--innerhtml` | No | Not implemented |
| `-0` / `--null` | No | Not implemented; useful for `xargs -0` workflows |
| `~` general sibling operator | No | Selector handling supports `+` and `>` currently (`selector.go`) |
| `-q` / `--quiet` | No | Not implemented; could imply `--exit-status` |
| `--pretty` | No | Tree display exists but not full HTML re-serialization |
| `--each` | No | Not implemented; would apply per-node selectors |
